Evaluation of the "Registration Procedure for Initial Registration" Flow
I have analyzed the provided JSON, which represents a procedural flow graph for the 3GPP NAS Registration Procedure for Initial Registration. Below is my evaluation based on correctness, completeness, and consistency with 3GPP TS 24.501 standards.

Strengths (Correct Aspects)
✅ Accurate Sequence of Events:

The initial registration process is correctly initiated from 5GMM-DEREGISTERED state.

The UE stops timers (T3502, T3511) before sending a REGISTRATION REQUEST.

The UE starts timers T3510 and T3519 (conditionally for SUCI) after sending the request.

AMF processing steps (common procedures, acceptance/rejection decision) are correctly included.

Conditional retransmissions and handling of T3550 expiry are correctly modeled.

Reject Handling: The UE correctly processes REGISTRATION REJECT, stops T3510, and follows actions based on the cause.

Retry Mechanism: Conditional retry logic is correctly implemented for T3511 and T3502.

✅ State Transitions & Timers Handling

States such as UE Registered, AMF Processing, UE Aborting Procedure are well-defined.

The conditional retransmission of REGISTRATION ACCEPT (T3550 expiry) aligns with 3GPP specs.

T3510 Expiry and Retry Mechanism (up to 5 attempts) are correctly included.

Identified Issues & Missing Elements
❌ Missing Authentication and Security Setup

3GPP TS 24.501 mandates that AMF may trigger authentication/security procedures before accepting registration.

The procedure lacks:

AMF Initiating Authentication Request (EAP-AKA, 5G-AKA, etc.)

UE Response with Authentication Response

Security Mode Command and UE Response

Key Agreement and Derivation

❌ Incorrect Handling of REGISTRATION COMPLETE Condition

REGISTRATION COMPLETE is not always required.

The JSON conditionally models REGISTRATION COMPLETE based on ACK requirements.

However, in some cases (e.g., no additional information needed), AMF does not require REGISTRATION COMPLETE.

❌ PLMN Search Handling Is Simplified

PLMN Search should occur earlier when the UE determines no suitable network.

Current implementation only triggers PLMN search after reject processing, which does not align with all possible failure cases.

❌ Failure Handling for AMF Response Timeout

If AMF does not respond within T3510 timeout, UE should take different actions (retry, select another PLMN, deregister, etc.).

The current model only focuses on incrementing attempt counters without fully detailing alternative actions.

